IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bgg3-nouns`
IMPORT `bgg3-civil`
IMPORT `bgg3-criminal`
IMPORT `bgg3-public-scope`
IMPORT `bgg3-public-limits`
IMPORT `bgg3-public-courts`

-- Federal Supreme Court Act (BGG, SR 173.110), chapter 3 (Art. 72 to 89): the Federal Supreme Court
-- as the ordinary appeal instance.  THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person affected by a decision: a party to civil or criminal proceedings, or to proceedings
-- in a public-law matter, who lost, or a person with another interest the text names.  They ask, on
-- facts they can state, whether they may appeal to the Federal Supreme Court, which appeal it is,
-- whether the value in dispute is enough, whether they have standing, which decisions are excluded
-- from appeal, and whether the case must first have gone through the cantons' highest instance.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the modules imported above as the questions that
-- person would ask about their own decision.  Nothing here is new law, and no layer-1 module was
-- changed for it.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Every question takes plain inputs (yes/no, numbers, and the modules' own choices:
-- the body that decided, the kind of decision), one for each fact the person can state, each with
-- an @desc worded as the person would be asked.  Where a question calls a module rule, it passes
-- the answers straight through; no rule is restated.
--
-- WHAT AN ANSWER MEANS (the rule of 2026-10-29, see NOTES.md, section Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING).
-- Every question answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING.
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes to these facts.
--   JUST FALSE  the text itself says no to these facts, in its own words.
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide these facts: it is silent, lists without closing the list,
--               leaves a term undefined, sends the question to another statute outside the sources
--               (chapters 4 ff., the Federal Constitution, the procedure codes), or limits its own
--               rule and the case falls outside the limit.  NOTHING is not "no".
-- The one exception to the rule that a question keeps the polarity of its module is Art 83, which is asked the way a person asks
-- it (is my decision excluded?): see its comment.
--
-- NOT IN THIS LAYER (layer 1 only, because they address an authority and not the person affected):
-- Art 76(2), 81(2), 81(3), 89(2)(a) and 89(2)(b) (which federal authority may appeal), and the three
-- duties and the one permission the cantons carry (Art 75(2), 80(2), 86(2), 86(3), 88(2) as
-- regulative rules); the person meets each of those through the decision function asked below.

§ `Federal Supreme Court Act, chapter 3 -- the questions of a person affected by a decision`

§§ `Civil matters (Art 72 to 77)`

-- Art 72.  Civil matters (Zivilsachen) is the text's term, not defined in this chapter: the person states whether it is one.
@export Can I appeal to the Federal Supreme Court in a civil matter against my decision (Art 72)?
GIVEN `my case is a civil matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your case a civil-law dispute (a matter of private law)?
      `my case is a debt enforcement or bankruptcy matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your case about debt enforcement or bankruptcy?
      `the decision I challenge is a public-law decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision you challenge a public-law decision (made by an authority as such)?
      `my public-law decision is in immediate connection with civil law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that public-law decision stand in immediate connection with civil law? (answer no if it is not a public-law decision)
      `the kind of my public-law decision` IS A `Kind of public-law decision listed in Art 72(2)(b)` @desc Which kind of public-law decision is it? (choose "another kind of decision" if none of the listed kinds fits)
      `my foundation is a pension or vested-benefits institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the decision is about supervising a foundation: is it a pension or vested-benefits institution? (otherwise answer no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 72 the appeal in civil matters lies against my decision` MEANS
    `Art 72 the appeal in civil matters lies against the decision`
        `my case is a civil matter`
        `my case is a debt enforcement or bankruptcy matter`
        `the decision I challenge is a public-law decision`
        `my public-law decision is in immediate connection with civil law`
        `the kind of my public-law decision`
        `my foundation is a pension or vested-benefits institution`

-- Art 73.
-- POLARITY SWAP (independent reader, 2026-11-18).  Layer 1 answers in the text's polarity: Art 73 is a bar ("Die Beschwerde ist unzulässig gegen Entscheide, die im Rahmen des Widerspruchsverfahrens gegen eine Marke getroffen worden sind"),
-- so layer 1 says JUST FALSE for a trade-mark opposition decision and NOTHING for every other decision.  A person asks about the bar, so this question swaps the two definite answers and leaves NOTHING alone:
--   JUST TRUE  = yes, the Act excludes my decision from the appeal (layer 1 said JUST FALSE);
--   JUST FALSE = no, the text itself lets my decision in (layer 1 said JUST TRUE: it never does for Art 73, so this arm is not reached today and keeps the swap total, as in Art 83);
--   NOTHING    = Art 73 does not decide my case (my decision was not made in opposition proceedings against a trade mark).
@export Is my civil-law decision one that the Act excludes from the appeal because it was made in trade-mark opposition proceedings (Art 73)?
GIVEN `my decision was made in opposition proceedings against a trade mark` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the decision made in opposition proceedings against a trade mark?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 73 my decision is excluded from the appeal in civil matters` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 73 the appeal in civil matters is admissible against the decision` `my decision was made in opposition proceedings against a trade mark`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE       -- the bar: "Die Beschwerde ist unzulässig gegen Entscheide, die im Rahmen des Widerspruchsverfahrens gegen eine Marke getroffen worden sind" (layer 1 holds the quoted words)
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE       -- POLARITY SWAP: not reached today (layer 1 never says JUST TRUE for Art 73); no text is quoted here
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar reaches only trade mark opposition decisions

-- Art 74(1): the value in dispute.  Francs; how the value is worked out is outside this chapter (chapter 4).
@export Is the value in dispute in my civil case enough for an appeal (Art 74(1))?
GIVEN `my case is a pecuniary matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the dispute about money or something worth money (a pecuniary matter)?
      `my case is an employment law case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an employment law case?
      `my case is a tenancy law case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a tenancy law case?
      `the value in dispute in francs` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value in dispute, in Swiss francs?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(1) the value in dispute in my case is enough` MEANS
    `Art 74(1) the value in dispute is enough`
        `my case is a pecuniary matter`
        `my case is an employment law case`
        `my case is a tenancy law case`
        `the value in dispute in francs`

-- Art 74(2): the value is short, but an appeal may still be admissible.
@export Can I still appeal in my civil case although the value in dispute is short (Art 74(2))?
GIVEN `my case is a pecuniary matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the dispute about money or something worth money (a pecuniary matter)?
      `my case is an employment law case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an employment law case?
      `my case is a tenancy law case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a tenancy law case?
      `the value in dispute in francs` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value in dispute, in Swiss francs?
      `my case raises a legal question of fundamental importance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your case raise a legal question of fundamental importance?
      `a federal statute provides for a single cantonal instance in my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a federal statute provide for a single cantonal instance in your kind of case?
      `my decision is of a cantonal supervisory authority in debt enforcement or bankruptcy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the decision made by a cantonal supervisory authority in a debt enforcement or bankruptcy matter?
      `my decision is of the bankruptcy and composition judge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the decision made by the bankruptcy and composition judge?
      `the body that made my decision` IS A `Deciding body` @desc Which body made the decision you challenge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(2) the appeal is admissible in my case although the value is short` MEANS
    `Art 74(2) the appeal is admissible although the value is short`
        `my case is a pecuniary matter`
        `my case is an employment law case`
        `my case is a tenancy law case`
        `the value in dispute in francs`
        `my case raises a legal question of fundamental importance`
        `a federal statute provides for a single cantonal instance in my case`
        `my decision is of a cantonal supervisory authority in debt enforcement or bankruptcy`
        `my decision is of the bankruptcy and composition judge`
        `the body that made my decision`

-- Art 75(1): the decision must be of the highest cantonal instance, or of the Federal Patent Court.
@export Can I appeal in my civil case against the decision of the body that made it (Art 75(1))?
GIVEN `the body that made my decision` IS A `Deciding body` @desc Which body made the decision you challenge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75(1) the appeal in civil matters is admissible against the decision of my lower instance` MEANS
    `Art 75(1) the appeal in civil matters is admissible against the decision of this body` `the body that made my decision`

-- Art 75(2): must my case first have gone through the cantons' highest instance?
@export Is my last cantonal instance the kind of court Art 75(2) requires, or does an exception apply (Art 75(2))?
GIVEN `my last cantonal instance is an upper court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the last cantonal instance an upper court?
      `my last cantonal instance decided as an appeal instance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it decide as an appeal instance?
      `a federal statute provides for a single cantonal instance in my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a federal statute provide for a single cantonal instance in your kind of case?
      `a specialised commercial court decided my case as the single cantonal instance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a specialised commercial court decide your case as the single cantonal instance?
      `my action was filed directly with the upper court with the consent of all parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your action filed directly with the upper court, with the consent of all parties?
      `the value in dispute in francs` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value in dispute, in Swiss francs?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75(2) my last cantonal instance is an upper court deciding as an appeal instance, or an exception applies` MEANS
    `Art 75(2) the last cantonal instance is an upper court deciding as an appeal instance, or an exception applies`
        `my last cantonal instance is an upper court`
        `my last cantonal instance decided as an appeal instance`
        `a federal statute provides for a single cantonal instance in my case`
        `a specialised commercial court decided my case as the single cantonal instance`
        `my action was filed directly with the upper court with the consent of all parties`
        `the value in dispute in francs`

-- Art 76(1): standing in civil matters.
@export Am I entitled to appeal in my civil case (Art 76(1))?
GIVEN `I took part in the proceedings before the lower instance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you take part in the proceedings before the lower instance?
      `I had no chance to take part before the lower instance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you did not take part: did you have no chance to take part?
      `I am especially affected by the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision affect you especially?
      `I have an interest worthy of protection in its quashing or change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have an interest worthy of protection in having the decision quashed or changed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 76(1) I am entitled to appeal in civil matters` MEANS
    `Art 76(1) the person is entitled to appeal in civil matters`
        `I took part in the proceedings before the lower instance`
        `I had no chance to take part before the lower instance`
        `I am especially affected by the decision`
        `I have an interest worthy of protection in its quashing or change`

-- Art 77(1): an arbitral award.
@export Can I appeal in a civil matter against an arbitral award, whatever the value in dispute (Art 77(1))?
GIVEN `my decision is of an arbitral tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the decision made by an arbitral tribunal?
      `my arbitration is international` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the arbitration international?
      `my arbitration is national` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the arbitration national?
      `the conditions of Arts 190 to 192 of the Private International Law Act are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the conditions of Arts 190 to 192 of the Private International Law Act met? (that Act is outside this chapter: say what you know)
      `the conditions of Arts 389 to 395 of the Civil Procedure Code are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the conditions of Arts 389 to 395 of the Civil Procedure Code met? (that Code is outside this chapter: say what you know)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 77(1) the appeal in civil matters is admissible against my arbitral award whatever the value in dispute` MEANS
    `Art 77(1) the appeal in civil matters is admissible against the arbitral award whatever the value in dispute`
        `my decision is of an arbitral tribunal`
        `my arbitration is international`
        `my arbitration is national`
        `the conditions of Arts 190 to 192 of the Private International Law Act are met`
        `the conditions of Arts 389 to 395 of the Civil Procedure Code are met`

-- Art 77(2): which provisions apply to the appeal against the award.
@export Does a given provision of the Act apply to my appeal against the arbitral award (Art 77(2))?
GIVEN `my appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal against an arbitral award that Art 77(1) allows?
      `the article number of the provision` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of the provision of the Act you ask about (for example 95)?
      `the paragraph number of the provision` IS A NUMBER @desc Which paragraph of that provision (0 if the provision has none, or you mean the whole article)?
      `the provision is used to let the Court decide the matter itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision one that would let the Federal Supreme Court decide the matter itself (and not send it back)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 77(2) the listed provision is applicable to my appeal against the arbitral award` MEANS
    `Art 77(2) the listed provision is applicable to the appeal against the arbitral award`
        `my appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)`
        `the article number of the provision`
        `the paragraph number of the provision`
        `the provision is used to let the Court decide the matter itself`

-- Art 77(2bis).
@export May I draft my written submission in English in my appeal against an arbitral award (Art 77(2bis))?
GIVEN `my appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal against an arbitral award that Art 77(1) allows?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 77(2bis) I may draft my written submission in English` MEANS
    `Art 77(2bis) the written submission may be drafted in English` `my appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)`

-- Art 77(3).
@export Will the Court examine my complaint against the arbitral award (Art 77(3))?
GIVEN `my appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal against an arbitral award that Art 77(1) allows?
      `I raised the complaint in my appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you raise the complaint in your appeal?
      `I gave reasons for the complaint in my appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give reasons for the complaint in your appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 77(3) my complaint meets the condition for being examined` MEANS
    `Art 77(3) the complaint meets the condition for being examined`
        `my appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)`
        `I raised the complaint in my appeal`
        `I gave reasons for the complaint in my appeal`

§§ `Criminal matters (Art 78 to 81)`

-- Art 78.
@export Can I appeal to the Federal Supreme Court in a criminal matter against my decision (Art 78)?
GIVEN `my case is a criminal matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your case a criminal matter?
      `my decision is on civil claims` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision a decision on civil claims?
      `my civil claims are dealt with together with the criminal matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are those civil claims dealt with together with the criminal matter?
      `my decision is on the execution of penalties and measures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision about the execution of penalties and measures?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 78 the appeal in criminal matters lies against my decision` MEANS
    `Art 78 the appeal in criminal matters lies against the decision`
        `my case is a criminal matter`
        `my decision is on civil claims`
        `my civil claims are dealt with together with the criminal matter`
        `my decision is on the execution of penalties and measures`

-- Art 79.
-- POLARITY SWAP (independent reader, 2026-11-18).  Art 79 is a bar on decisions of the Complaints Chamber that are NOT about a coercive measure
-- ("Die Beschwerde ist unzulässig gegen Entscheide der Beschwerdekammer des Bundesstrafgerichts, soweit es sich nicht um Entscheide über Zwangsmassnahmen handelt").
-- Layer 1 answers in the text's polarity: JUST FALSE for a Complaints Chamber decision that is not on a coercive measure, NOTHING for every other decision (including one that IS on a coercive measure).
-- A person asks about the bar, so this question swaps the two definite answers and leaves NOTHING alone:
--   JUST TRUE  = yes, the Act excludes my decision from the appeal (layer 1 said JUST FALSE);
--   JUST FALSE = no, the text itself lets my decision in (layer 1 said JUST TRUE: it never does for Art 79, so this arm is not reached today and keeps the swap total);
--   NOTHING    = Art 79 does not decide my case (the decision is not of the Complaints Chamber, or it is on a coercive measure).
-- A decision on a coercive measure answers NOTHING, not JUST FALSE: the text does not say that such an appeal is admissible, here (Art 80(1) is the section that speaks to it).
@export Is my criminal-matter decision of the Complaints Chamber excluded from the appeal because it is not about a coercive measure (Art 79)?
GIVEN `the body that made my decision` IS A `Deciding body` @desc Which body made the decision you challenge? (this question is about decisions of the Complaints Chamber of the Federal Criminal Court; for any other body the answer is not covered)
      `my decision is on coercive measures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision about coercive measures?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 79 my decision of the Complaints Chamber is excluded from the appeal in criminal matters` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 79 the appeal in criminal matters is admissible against the decision of this body` `the body that made my decision` `my decision is on coercive measures`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE       -- the bar: "Die Beschwerde ist unzulässig gegen Entscheide der Beschwerdekammer des Bundesstrafgerichts, soweit es sich nicht um Entscheide über Zwangsmassnahmen handelt" (layer 1 holds the quoted words)
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE       -- POLARITY SWAP: not reached today (layer 1 never says JUST TRUE for Art 79); no text is quoted here
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar reaches only Complaints Chamber decisions that are not on a coercive measure

-- Art 80(1): the decision must be of the last cantonal instance or of a Federal Criminal Court chamber.
@export Can I appeal in my criminal case against the decision of the body that made it (Art 80(1))?
GIVEN `the body that made my decision` IS A `Deciding body` @desc Which body made the decision you challenge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 80(1) the appeal in criminal matters is admissible against the decision of my lower instance` MEANS
    `Art 80(1) the appeal in criminal matters is admissible against the decision of this body` `the body that made my decision`

-- Art 80(2): must my case first have gone through the cantons' highest instance?
@export Is my last cantonal instance the kind of court Art 80(2) requires, or does the exception apply (Art 80(2))?
GIVEN `my last cantonal instance is an upper court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the last cantonal instance an upper court?
      `my last cantonal instance decided as an appeal instance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it decide as an appeal instance?
      `under the Code of Criminal Procedure an upper court or a court for coercive measures decides my case as the single cantonal instance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Code of Criminal Procedure have an upper court or a court for coercive measures decide your kind of case as the single cantonal instance? (that Code is outside this chapter: say what you know)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 80(2) my last cantonal instance is an upper court deciding as an appeal instance, or the exception applies` MEANS
    `Art 80(2) the last cantonal instance is an upper court deciding as an appeal instance, or the exception applies`
        `my last cantonal instance is an upper court`
        `my last cantonal instance decided as an appeal instance`
        `under the Code of Criminal Procedure an upper court or a court for coercive measures decides my case as the single cantonal instance`

-- Art 81(1): standing in criminal matters.
@export Am I entitled to appeal in my criminal case (Art 81(1))?
GIVEN `I took part in the proceedings before the lower instance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you take part in the proceedings before the lower instance?
      `I had no chance to take part before the lower instance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you did not take part: did you have no chance to take part?
      `my role in the criminal appeal` IS A `Person in a criminal appeal` @desc What is your role? (the accused person, the accused person's legal representative, the public prosecutor's office, the private claimant, the person who files the criminal complaint, the federal public prosecutor's office or the administration involved, or another person)
      `my decision is on ordering, prolonging or lifting investigative or security detention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision about ordering, prolonging or lifting investigative or security detention?
      `my decision can affect the assessment of my civil claims as private claimant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are a private claimant: can the decision affect the assessment of your civil claims?
      `my appeal concerns the right to file a criminal complaint as such` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you filed the complaint: does your appeal concern the right to file a criminal complaint as such?
      `I have a legally protected interest in the quashing or change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are another person: do you have a legally protected interest in having the decision quashed or changed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 81(1) I am entitled to appeal in criminal matters` MEANS
    `Art 81(1) the person is entitled to appeal in criminal matters`
        `I took part in the proceedings before the lower instance`
        `I had no chance to take part before the lower instance`
        `my role in the criminal appeal`
        `my decision is on ordering, prolonging or lifting investigative or security detention`
        `my decision can affect the assessment of my civil claims as private claimant`
        `my appeal concerns the right to file a criminal complaint as such`
        `I have a legally protected interest in the quashing or change`

§§ `Public-law matters (Art 82 to 89)`

-- Art 82.
@export Can I appeal to the Federal Supreme Court in a public-law matter (Art 82)?
GIVEN `my decision is in a matter of public law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision in a matter of public law?
      `the act I challenge is a cantonal enactment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you challenge a cantonal enactment (a cantonal statute or ordinance) as such?
      `my appeal concerns my political voting rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your appeal concern the political voting rights of citizens?
      `my appeal concerns a popular election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your appeal concern a popular election?
      `my appeal concerns a popular vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your appeal concern a popular vote?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 82 the appeal in public-law matters lies against my decision` MEANS
    `Art 82 the appeal in public-law matters lies`
        `my decision is in a matter of public law`
        `the act I challenge is a cantonal enactment`
        `my appeal concerns my political voting rights`
        `my appeal concerns a popular election`
        `my appeal concerns a popular vote`

-- Art 83: the text lists the decisions against which the appeal is NOT admissible.  Layer 1 answers
-- the question in the text's own polarity (JUST FALSE = the appeal is barred).  A person asks the
-- other way round, so this question swaps the two definite answers and leaves NOTHING alone:
--   JUST TRUE  = yes, the list excludes my decision (layer 1 said JUST FALSE);
--   JUST FALSE = no, the text itself lets the appeal in (layer 1 said JUST TRUE: only limb (m), "in Abweichung davon ... zulässig");
--   NOTHING    = no limb of the list decides the case.
-- The kind of decision is the person's one choice; the facts below are asked only for the kinds they belong to,
-- and a fact that does not belong to the chosen kind is not read (answer no, or 0).
@export Is my decision one that the Act excludes from the appeal in public-law matters (Art 83)?
GIVEN `the kind of my decision` IS A `Art 83 kind of decision` @desc Which kind of decision is yours? (choose "none of these kinds" if none fits)
      `international law gives me a claim to judicial review` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for decisions on security, neutrality, diplomatic protection or foreign affairs: does international law give you a claim to judicial review? (otherwise no)
      `federal law or international law gives me a claim to the permit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for permits in foreigners law or asylum law: does federal law or international law give you a claim to the permit? (otherwise no)
      `an extradition request against me is pending from the state where I seek refuge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for asylum decisions of the Federal Administrative Court: is an extradition request pending against you from the state before which you seek protection? (otherwise no)
      `the Federal Administrative Court made my decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Federal Administrative Court make your decision?
      `a cantonal lower instance made my decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a cantonal lower instance make your decision?
      `my case raises a legal question of fundamental importance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your case raise a legal question of fundamental importance?
      `the procuring body is one of those that Art 83(f)(1) reserves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for public procurement: is the procuring body the Federal Administrative Court, the Federal Criminal Court, the Federal Patent Court, the Office of the Attorney General, or an upper cantonal court? (otherwise no)
      `the estimated value of the contract to be awarded` IS A NUMBER @desc Only for public procurement: what is the estimated value of the contract to be awarded, in Swiss francs? (otherwise 0)
      `the threshold under the Public Procurement Act` IS A NUMBER @desc Only for public procurement: what is the threshold under the Public Procurement Act for this kind of contract, in Swiss francs? (that Act is outside this chapter; otherwise 0)
      `my matter is not pecuniary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for public-law employment: is the matter not about money? (otherwise no)
      `my matter concerns equality of the sexes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for public-law employment: does the matter concern equality of the sexes? (otherwise no)
      `the assistance is in tax matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for international administrative assistance: is it assistance in tax matters? (otherwise no)
      `my remission concerns the direct federal tax or a cantonal or communal income or profit tax` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for remission of levies: does the remission concern the direct federal tax or a cantonal or communal income or profit tax? (otherwise no)
      `my case is particularly important for other reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your case particularly important for reasons other than a legal question of fundamental importance?
      `my decision was taken in a severe shortage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for economic national supply: was the decision taken in a severe shortage? (otherwise no)
      `a claim to my subsidy exists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for subsidies: does a claim to the subsidy exist? (otherwise no)
      `my customs assessment rests on tariff classification or on the weight of the goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for customs assessments: does the assessment rest on tariff classification or on the weight of the goods? (otherwise no)
      `my concession was the subject of a public tender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for concessions in telecommunications, radio, television and post: was the concession the subject of a public tender? (otherwise no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 83 my decision is excluded from the appeal in public-law matters` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 83 the appeal is admissible against the decision` `the kind of my decision` `my facts`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE       -- the list says the appeal is inadmissible: "Die Beschwerde ist unzulässig gegen:" (layer 1 holds the quoted words of each limb)
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE       -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in Abweichung davon ist die Beschwerde zulässig gegen Entscheide über den Erlass der direkten Bundessteuer" (limb (m)'s departure; layer 1 quotes the German)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): no limb of Art 83 decides these facts
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `Art 83 facts` WITH
            `international law gives a claim to judicial review` IS `international law gives me a claim to judicial review`
            `federal law or international law gives a claim to the permit` IS `federal law or international law gives me a claim to the permit`
            `an extradition request is pending from the state of refuge` IS `an extradition request against me is pending from the state where I seek refuge`
            `the Federal Administrative Court decided` IS `the Federal Administrative Court made my decision`
            `a cantonal lower instance decided` IS `a cantonal lower instance made my decision`
            `a legal question of fundamental importance arises` IS `my case raises a legal question of fundamental importance`
            `the procuring body is one that item (f)(1) reserves` IS `the procuring body is one of those that Art 83(f)(1) reserves`
            `the estimated value of the contract to be awarded` IS `the estimated value of the contract to be awarded`
            `the threshold under the Public Procurement Act` IS `the threshold under the Public Procurement Act`
            `the matter is not pecuniary` IS `my matter is not pecuniary`
            `the matter concerns equality of the sexes` IS `my matter concerns equality of the sexes`
            `the assistance is in tax matters` IS `the assistance is in tax matters`
            `the remission concerns the direct federal tax or a cantonal or communal income or profit tax` IS `my remission concerns the direct federal tax or a cantonal or communal income or profit tax`
            `the case is particularly important for other reasons` IS `my case is particularly important for other reasons`
            `the decision was taken in a severe shortage` IS `my decision was taken in a severe shortage`
            `a claim to the subsidy exists` IS `a claim to my subsidy exists`
            `the customs assessment rests on tariff classification or on the weight of the goods` IS `my customs assessment rests on tariff classification or on the weight of the goods`
            `the concession was the subject of a public tender` IS `my concession was the subject of a public tender`

-- Art 84(1) with Art 84(2): international legal assistance in criminal matters.
@export In international legal assistance in criminal matters, is my case one in which an appeal is admissible (Art 84)?
GIVEN `my decision is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters?
      `the subject of my decision` IS A `Subject of a legal assistance decision` @desc What does the decision concern? (extradition, seizure, handing over of objects or assets, transmission of information from the secret sphere, or another subject)
      `there are grounds to assume that elementary procedural principles were violated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there grounds to assume that elementary procedural principles were violated in the proceedings abroad?
      `there are grounds to assume that the proceedings abroad have serious defects` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there grounds to assume that the proceedings abroad have serious defects in other respects?
      `my case is particularly important for other reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your case particularly important for other reasons?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 84(1) the condition for an appeal on international legal assistance in criminal matters is met in my case` MEANS
    `Art 84(1) the condition for an appeal on international legal assistance in criminal matters is met`
        `my decision is in the field of international legal assistance in criminal matters`
        `the subject of my decision`
        `there are grounds to assume that elementary procedural principles were violated`
        `there are grounds to assume that the proceedings abroad have serious defects`
        `my case is particularly important for other reasons`

-- Art 84a: international administrative assistance in tax matters.
@export In international administrative assistance in tax matters, is my case one in which an appeal is admissible (Art 84a)?
GIVEN `my decision is in the field of international administrative assistance in tax matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision in the field of international administrative assistance in tax matters?
      `my case raises a legal question of fundamental importance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your case raise a legal question of fundamental importance?
      `there are grounds to assume that elementary procedural principles were violated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there grounds to assume that elementary procedural principles were violated in the proceedings abroad?
      `there are grounds to assume that the proceedings abroad have serious defects` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there grounds to assume that the proceedings abroad have serious defects in other respects?
      `my case is particularly important for other reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your case particularly important for other reasons?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 84a the condition for an appeal on international administrative assistance in tax matters is met in my case` MEANS
    `Art 84a the condition for an appeal on international administrative assistance in tax matters is met`
        `my decision is in the field of international administrative assistance in tax matters`
        `my case raises a legal question of fundamental importance`
        `there are grounds to assume that elementary procedural principles were violated`
        `there are grounds to assume that the proceedings abroad have serious defects`
        `my case is particularly important for other reasons`

-- Art 85(1): the value thresholds in a pecuniary public-law matter.
@export Is the value in dispute in my public-law money matter enough for an appeal (Art 85(1))?
GIVEN `my matter is a pecuniary matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter about money or something worth money (a pecuniary matter)?
      `my matter is in the field of state liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter in the field of state liability?
      `my matter is in the field of public-law employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter in the field of public-law employment?
      `the value in dispute in francs` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value in dispute, in Swiss francs?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 85(1) the appeal is admissible in my pecuniary matter` MEANS
    `Art 85(1) the appeal is admissible in a pecuniary matter`
        `my matter is a pecuniary matter`
        `my matter is in the field of state liability`
        `my matter is in the field of public-law employment`
        `the value in dispute in francs`

-- Art 85(2): the value is short, but an appeal may still be admissible.
@export Can I still appeal in my public-law money matter although the value in dispute is short (Art 85(2))?
GIVEN `my matter is a pecuniary matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter about money or something worth money (a pecuniary matter)?
      `my matter is in the field of state liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter in the field of state liability?
      `my matter is in the field of public-law employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter in the field of public-law employment?
      `the value in dispute in francs` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value in dispute, in Swiss francs?
      `my case raises a legal question of fundamental importance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your case raise a legal question of fundamental importance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 85(2) the appeal is admissible in my case although the value is short` MEANS
    `Art 85(2) the appeal is admissible although the value is short`
        `my matter is a pecuniary matter`
        `my matter is in the field of state liability`
        `my matter is in the field of public-law employment`
        `the value in dispute in francs`
        `my case raises a legal question of fundamental importance`

-- Art 86(1): the decision must come from one of the named bodies.
@export Can I appeal in my public-law case against the decision of the body that made it (Art 86(1))?
GIVEN `the body that made my decision` IS A `Deciding body` @desc Which body made the decision you challenge?
      `an appeal to the Federal Administrative Court is admissible in my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an appeal to the Federal Administrative Court admissible against your decision? (that follows from other statutes; say what you know)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 86(1) the appeal in public-law matters is admissible against the decision of my lower instance` MEANS
    `Art 86(1) the appeal in public-law matters is admissible against the decision of this body` `the body that made my decision` `an appeal to the Federal Administrative Court is admissible in my case`

-- Art 86(2): must my case first have gone through an upper court?
@export Is my immediate lower instance an upper court, or does another federal statute provide for an appeal from the other judicial authority (Art 86(2))?
GIVEN `my immediate lower instance is an upper court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the immediate lower instance an upper court?
      `under another federal statute decisions of another judicial authority in my case are subject to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another federal statute let decisions of another judicial authority be appealed to the Federal Supreme Court in your kind of case? (that statute is outside this chapter: say what you know)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 86(2) my immediate lower instance is an upper court, or another federal statute provides for appeal from another judicial authority` MEANS
    `Art 86(2) the immediate lower instance is an upper court, or another federal statute provides for appeal from another judicial authority`
        `my immediate lower instance is an upper court`
        `under another federal statute decisions of another judicial authority in my case are subject to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court`

-- Art 86(3): the canton's power, seen from the person whose decision came from a non-court authority.
@export Could my canton lawfully have used an authority that is not a court as the immediate lower instance in my case (Art 86(3))?
GIVEN `my decision is of predominantly political character` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision of predominantly political character?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 86(3) my canton may have set up an authority other than a court as immediate lower instance` MEANS
    `Art 86(3) the canton may set up an authority other than a court as immediate lower instance` `my decision is of predominantly political character`

-- Art 87(1): a challenge to a cantonal enactment.
@export Can I appeal directly to the Federal Supreme Court against a cantonal enactment (Art 87(1))?
GIVEN `the act I challenge is a cantonal enactment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you challenge a cantonal enactment (a cantonal statute or ordinance) as such?
      `a cantonal remedy can be taken against it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can a cantonal remedy be taken against the enactment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 87(1) the appeal lies directly against the cantonal enactment I challenge` MEANS
    `Art 87(1) the appeal lies directly against the cantonal enactment` `the act I challenge is a cantonal enactment` `a cantonal remedy can be taken against it`

-- Art 87(2): where cantonal law provides a remedy against enactments.
@export Where my canton gives a remedy against enactments, does Art 86 apply to my appeal (Art 87(2))?
GIVEN `the act I challenge is a cantonal enactment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you challenge a cantonal enactment (a cantonal statute or ordinance) as such?
      `cantonal law provides a remedy against enactments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does cantonal law provide a remedy against enactments?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 87(2) Art 86 applies to my appeal against the cantonal enactment` MEANS
    `Art 87(2) Art 86 applies to the appeal against the cantonal enactment` `the act I challenge is a cantonal enactment` `cantonal law provides a remedy against enactments`

-- Art 88(1): voting rights matters.
@export In a voting rights matter, can I appeal against the act I challenge (Art 88(1))?
GIVEN `my appeal concerns political voting rights, a popular election or a popular vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your appeal concern political voting rights, a popular election or a popular vote?
      `my matter is a cantonal matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a cantonal matter?
      `the act I challenge is an act of the last cantonal instance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act you challenge an act of the last cantonal instance?
      `my matter is a federal matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a federal matter?
      `the act I challenge is a ruling of the Federal Chancellery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act you challenge a ruling of the Federal Chancellery?
      `the act I challenge is a decision of a cantonal government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act you challenge a decision of a cantonal government?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 88(1) the appeal on voting rights is admissible against the act I challenge` MEANS
    `Art 88(1) the appeal on voting rights is admissible against the act`
        `my appeal concerns political voting rights, a popular election or a popular vote`
        `my matter is a cantonal matter`
        `the act I challenge is an act of the last cantonal instance`
        `my matter is a federal matter`
        `the act I challenge is a ruling of the Federal Chancellery`
        `the act I challenge is a decision of a cantonal government`

-- Art 88(2): the canton's duty to give a remedy, seen from the voter.
@export Must my canton give me a remedy against an act that can violate my political rights (Art 88(2))?
GIVEN `the act can violate my political rights in a cantonal matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the act violate the political rights of voters in a cantonal matter?
      `the act is an act of the parliament or the government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act an act of the parliament or of the government?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 88(2) my canton must provide a remedy against the act` MEANS
    `Art 88(2) the canton must provide a remedy against the act` `the act can violate my political rights in a cantonal matter` `the act is an act of the parliament or the government`

-- Art 89(1): standing in public-law matters.
@export Am I entitled to appeal in my public-law case (Art 89(1))?
GIVEN `I took part in the proceedings before the lower instance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you take part in the proceedings before the lower instance?
      `I had no chance to take part before the lower instance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you did not take part: did you have no chance to take part?
      `I am especially affected by the decision or enactment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision or enactment affect you especially?
      `I have an interest worthy of protection in its quashing or change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have an interest worthy of protection in having it quashed or changed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 89(1) I am entitled to appeal in public-law matters` MEANS
    `Art 89(1) the person is entitled to appeal in public-law matters`
        `I took part in the proceedings before the lower instance`
        `I had no chance to take part before the lower instance`
        `I am especially affected by the decision or enactment`
        `I have an interest worthy of protection in its quashing or change`

-- Art 89(2)(c): a municipality or other public-law corporation.
@export As a municipality or other public-law corporation, am I also entitled to appeal (Art 89(2)(c))?
GIVEN `I am a municipality or other public-law corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a municipality or another public-law corporation?
      `I complain of a violation of guarantees that the cantonal or federal constitution gives me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you complain of a violation of guarantees that the cantonal or federal constitution gives you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 89(2)(c) a municipality or other public-law corporation like me is also entitled to appeal` MEANS
    `Art 89(2)(c) the municipality or other public-law corporation is also entitled to appeal` `I am a municipality or other public-law corporation` `I complain of a violation of guarantees that the cantonal or federal constitution gives me`

-- Art 89(2)(d): another federal statute gives the right.
@export Does another federal statute give me the right to appeal (Art 89(2)(d))?
GIVEN `another federal statute gives me this right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another federal statute give you (a person, an organisation or an authority) the right to appeal? (that statute is outside this chapter: say what you know)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 89(2)(d) another federal statute may give me the right to appeal` MEANS
    `Art 89(2)(d) the person, organisation or authority is also entitled to appeal under another federal statute` `another federal statute gives me this right`

-- Art 89(3): voters in a voting rights matter.
@export As a voter, am I entitled to appeal in a voting rights matter (Art 89(3))?
GIVEN `my appeal is in a matter of voting rights (Art 82(c))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal in a matter of voting rights (political voting rights, popular elections or popular votes)?
      `I am entitled to vote in the matter concerned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to vote in the matter concerned?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 89(3) I am entitled to appeal in a voting rights matter as a voter` MEANS
    `Art 89(3) the person entitled to vote is also entitled to appeal in a voting rights matter` `my appeal is in a matter of voting rights (Art 82(c))` `I am entitled to vote in the matter concerned`
